          "answer": "Role-Based Access Control authorizes API actions through Roles, ClusterRoles and bindings.\n\nOperational responsibility:\nRBAC is used as part of the Kubernetes workflow. Understand its inputs, outputs, dependencies, permissions and failure conditions.\n\nPractical command or check:\nkubectl auth can-i get pods\n\nProduction problem:\nA deployment automation receives Forbidden.\n\nInvestigation:\nInspect service account, role rules, binding subject and namespace. Grant minimum required access and retest the exact API operation.\n\nVerification and prevention:\nConfirm the relevant service or resource is healthy, repeat the affected operation, inspect logs and metrics, and monitor after the change. Document the root cause and add an alert or preventive control.",
